/-
  LeanVM.Guest.Data.CplHand

  The completeness walk's instruction counts and set-up call site cells at each window's start,
  for the functions of several windows.
-/

module

public import LeanVM.Guest.Code

/-!
Window `i + 1` of function `j` starts with what window `i` ends with: the counts of each opcode
(in `Opcode`'s order) the walk's paths pass at most, and the bit set of the callee frame pointer
and dispatch target cells they set up. They are read off the kernel's evaluation of
`B2C.cplRes j i` window by window, and checked by `B2C.cplWin`; functions of one window start
with none.
-/

namespace LeanVM.Guest.Data

@[expose] public section

